<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Fok unit buys Hong Kong property.</title>
<headline>Hong Fok unit buys Hong Kong property.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified property company Hong Fok Corp Ltd said on Friday it had raised a Singapore $40 million loan and was investing S$34.5 million in a Hong Kong property through a wholly-owned subsidiary.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it was raising the transferable loan facility from Citibank over five years at six percent per year.</p>
<p>It said its unit Super Homes had agreed to buy a residential property in Hong Kong for redevelopment for HK$190 million (S$34.5 million). The agreement was struck on October 15 and the sale would be completed by January 1997, it said.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
